# 3. The second architectural gap: a late transcript is not a first-class event

The transcript repository remains optimized for live Meet-caption append.

`RecordingTranscriptService` has essentially:

```text
get
status
append
removeAll
```

`append()` refuses a source change.

The service itself explicitly says `processing` is currently unreachable.

[RecordingTranscriptService](https://github.com/kstroevsky/chrome-meeting-recording-extension/blob/feat/external-integrations-module/src/background/library/transcript/RecordingTranscriptService.ts?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

That was correct for PR #17.

It is not the contract we want before STT.

We want:

```text
caption source
        │
        ├──── append while recording
        │
        ▼
   commit transcript
        │
        ▼
analysis reconciliation

or

finished recording
        │
        ▼
STT eventually completes
        │
        ▼
   commit transcript
        │
        ▼
analysis reconciliation

or

user imports/replaces transcript
        │
        ▼
   commit transcript
        │
        ▼
analysis reconciliation
```

The important concept should therefore be **transcript commit**, not “recording finished.”

### Don't make a callback the correctness mechanism

It would be easy to write:

```ts
await transcripts.save(...);
await analysis.analyze(recordingId);
```

That is insufficient in MV3.

Chrome can kill the service worker between those two statements.

The repository already understands this principle elsewhere, so I would apply the same discipline:

```text
durable transcript revision committed
        │
        ▼
analysis becomes derivably dirty
        │
        ▼
fast-path notification
        +
bounded reconciliation
```

A transcript-commit notification can make the usual path immediate.

A startup/recovery reconciler makes it correct.

Something like:

```ts
ensureCurrentAnalysis(recordingId)
```

should become idempotent:

```text
no transcript          → no work
same fingerprint       → no work
job already active     → no work
analysis missing       → enqueue
analysis wrong input   → enqueue
analysis wrong config  → enqueue
```

This is an industry-standard reconciler shape and fits the existing repository much better than introducing an event-sourcing system.

### Race that needs a test

There is an especially important case:

```text
Transcript A
   ↓
Analysis A running

Transcript B committed before A finishes
   ↓

Analysis A result arrives
```

The result must never become the current analysis for B.

Once provenance carries `transcriptHash`, this is simple:

```text
A result input hash != current transcript hash
→ don't expose it as current
→ ensure B is scheduled
```

