# 4. External integrations make this correction more urgent

The new integration module raises the bar for consistency.

Its snapshot builder is intentionally a canonical-state projection:

```text
history
context
notations
transcript
analysis
artifacts
       ↓
IntegrationRecordingV1
```

That is a good design.

But several aggregates are currently fetched independently. Once transcripts become replaceable, an integration build can race a transcript update and observe a mixed logical revision.

You do not necessarily need to refactor the whole library into one transaction immediately. A transcript fingerprint already lets the builder detect the important inconsistency:

```text
transcript.contentHash = B

analysis.provenance.transcriptHash = A

→ snapshot is NOT analysis-ready
```

I would also stop translating a stale analysis into `unsupported`.

Those are semantically different:

```text
unsupported
= this machine/runtime cannot perform analysis

stale
= we deliberately need to recompute derived data
```

That distinction matters to external automation.

The clean model is closer to:

```text
readiness.pending = ['analysis']

analysis omitted / status stale
```

until the reconciler produces a B analysis.

