# 9. Reference-free evaluation can help before annotations exist

Two papers are useful here.

SegReFree introduced an embedding-based reference-free segmentation-quality measure. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="16"}

Ghinassi et al. 2024 subsequently proposed a broader embedding-space framework using Average Relative Proximity and showed strong correlations with traditional annotation-dependent metrics in many domains—although importantly, **conversation was the hardest domain**. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="17"}

I would therefore add one of these as a **regression signal**, not as ground truth.

That gives the development loop:

```text
algorithm change
     │
     ├── synthetic gold tests
     ├── public AMI gold tests
     ├── holdout
     └── reference-free cohesion regression
```

Later, when you run an unlabeled Russian call, you at least have a sanity metric before manual annotation exists.

