# 12. There are cheap dialogue features worth evaluating

Your current boundary score is:

```text
0.70 semantic
0.10 long pause
0.10 speaker-pattern change
0.10 discourse cue
```

The structure is sensible.

The current `speakerPatternChange`, however, is basically a Jaccard comparison of speaker sets.

That throws away:

```text
speaker frequency
dominant speaker
turn ordering
interruption pattern
```

The 2024 multi-party conversation study by Decker & Amblard specifically found linguistic/dialogue features useful for segmentation, including speaker structure and new-vocabulary behavior. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="22"}

I would experimentally add:

```text
speaker-distribution divergence
dominant-speaker switch
turn-transition rate
question → answer continuity
finite-memory vocabulary novelty
```

A Jensen–Shannon divergence over speaker distributions is probably a more useful candidate than set Jaccard.

Do not add all these to the production score.

Add them to the trace and calibration harness and see whether they have signal.

