# 13. Keyword cohesion is worth trying before another model

*Words That Stick* (CoNLL 2024) is unusually applicable to your constraints.

It remains unsupervised, uses strong embeddings plus representative keywords, retains a memory of earlier keywords, and improved unsupervised segmentation without fine-tuning. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="23"}

Your current pipeline calculates topic keywords only **after** segmentation.

An experimental variant can maintain a cheap lexical/keyphrase memory during segmentation:

```text
embedding change
+
keyword-cohesion change
```

This may help when embeddings put semantically adjacent but topically distinct technical discussions too close together.

Again: research lane first.

