# 15. The current importance score has two mathematical smells

Current passage importance combines:

```text
0.30 similarity_to_topic
0.25 novelty
0.20 keyword_distinctiveness
0.15 recurrence
0.10 discourse_signal
```

Two issues stand out.

First, `similarity_to_topic` and `recurrence` are closely related vector-space centrality measures. They are unlikely to be independent signals, so you may effectively be assigning ~45% of the score to “how central is this embedding?”

Second, the first passage receives maximal novelty by construction because it has no previous passage against which to compare.

That induces a positional prior:

```text
earlier == more novel
```

whether or not earlier is more important.

I would **not change the weights yet**, because we do not possess “important moment” ground truth.

Instead change observability:

```ts
importance: {
   total,
   similarity,
   novelty,
   keywordDistinctiveness,
   recurrence,
   discourse
}
```

in calibration/debug traces.

Then measure correlations.

If:

```text
corr(similarity, recurrence) = 0.9
```

we have empirical justification to redesign it later.

Representative excerpts still don't have a major product consumer, so this is not where I would spend most of the next sprint.

