# 17. Add metamorphic tests now

We don't need human topic labels for a whole category of powerful tests.

Examples:

```text
same transcript + all timestamps shifted by +1 hour
→ same topics

same text split into smaller adjacent chunks
→ approximately same macro topics

adjacent same-speaker chunks merged
→ approximately same macro topics

speaker labels removed
→ semantic structure remains plausible

punctuation removed
→ macro topics stable

"yes / right / uh-huh" injected
→ shouldn't create new topics

duplicate paraphrase inside same topic
→ shouldn't create new topic

tiny Float32 perturbations
→ shouldn't radically change graph
```

These tests exercise **invariants**, not gold labels.

For the future ASR pipeline, split/merge invariance is especially important.

