# 19. Preserve pause/audio information

The code was right to keep timestamps.

Do not collapse future STT output to plain text.

ACL 2026's *Beyond Transcripts* is particularly relevant here. It systematically compared text and audio chaptering and found that **pauses supplied the largest acoustic gains**, while transcript quality, duration and speaker composition also mattered. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="27"}

For eventual STT, retain:

```text
time
track/source
speaker if available
```

and leave room for acoustic features.

You don't need an acoustic segmentation model now.

Just don't design them out.

