# 20. Build an embedding cache boundary

The calibration script already follows a very good principle:

> Embed once; vary cheap arithmetic repeatedly.

Production does not fully exploit this.

If:

```text
assignmentThreshold changes
mergeThreshold changes
peak prominence changes
importance definition changes
```

the transcript embeddings themselves have not changed.

Yet analysis invalidation can require inference again.

Once transcript fingerprinting exists, I would introduce an **evictable derived embedding artifact**:

```text
key:
  transcriptHash
  analysisUnitVersion
  embeddingModel
  embeddingRevision
  dtype
  window specification

value:
  window metadata
  vectors
```

Then:

```text
Transcript
   ↓
embedding artifact   ← expensive
   ↓
segmentation         ← cheap
clustering           ← cheap
keywords             ← cheap
importance           ← cheap
```

This matters now because 4B is explicitly going to change arithmetic/configuration repeatedly.

It also makes experimentation with DP/global clustering extremely cheap.

It should be a cache, not canonical state.

Corruption/deletion of the cache must only cost recomputation.

