# 21. The embedding model itself does not need changing now

I also checked newer multilingual embedding work rather than assuming E5 remains optimal.

There are much newer models: Nomic Embed v2 is multilingual and has 475M total / 142M active parameters but reports around 1.8 GB memory; Jina v3 is ~570M parameters; BGE-M3 is also around 569M and ~2.27 GB. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="28"}

They are very interesting for a server.

They are much less obviously attractive for a Chrome extension whose current packaged Q8 E5 model was deliberately chosen for browser size and WASM fallback.

Multilingual-E5 itself was trained contrastively on a billion multilingual text pairs and has small/base/large variants explicitly designed around efficiency/quality tradeoffs. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="29"}

So I would **not reopen the embedding choice yet**.

Once the public corpus harness exists, adding one challenger is trivial—and then we can make the decision empirically instead of from MTEB retrieval numbers that don't directly measure meeting segmentation.

