# 22. We should also revise one old architectural assumption

The Plan B document still largely describes:

```text
live AudioWorklet
→ 16 kHz PCM sidecar
→ Whisper
```

That was a reasonable first design.

I no longer think we should build the sidecar first.

Without an ASR model, we can spike a cleaner abstraction:

```text
sealed recording artifact
       ↓
container demux / audio decode
       ↓
bounded audio frames
       ↓
AsyncIterable<AudioFrame>
       ↓
fake consumer
```

Where:

```ts
type AudioFrame = {
  samples: Float32Array;
  sampleRate: number;
  channels: number;
  tStartMs: number;
};
```

Crucially, don't hard-code 16 kHz into this generic stage.

The eventual model-specific audio frontend can request:

```text
16k
mono
resampling
VAD
overlap
```

if that's what the winning model needs.

The spike should prove:

```text
2–3h artifact does not become one huge ArrayBuffer
bounded memory
cancellation works
timestamps remain correct
pause/resume timeline is correct
separate mic/tab tracks work
decode faster than acceptable threshold
```

If that succeeds, we avoid:

```text
live recording overhead
temporary 100+ MB/hour PCM sidecar
extra cleanup/recovery path
```

and gain:

```text
retranscribe old recordings
```

Only if post-recording decoding proves operationally bad should the PCM sidecar return.

