# 24. Recommended sequence

I would implement the next work in this order:

1. **Derived-data correctness PR.** Add transcript revisions/fingerprints, carry the transcript fingerprint in analysis provenance, make transcript commit/replace first-class, invalidate analysis by input identity, make late transcript arrival schedule analysis, add bounded startup reconciliation, prevent old in-flight results from becoming current, and ensure integration snapshots never combine a transcript with analysis from another revision. This PR needs no model and no corpus.

2. **Analysis robustness/research-infrastructure PR.** Introduce the `AnalysisTurn` seam with identity behavior initially, add structured analysis tracing, add split/merge/chunk-shape metamorphic tests, add backchannel/noise corruption generators, improve metrics with Pk/WindowDiff/time boundary metrics/B³ or ARI, and bootstrap confidence intervals by meeting.

3. **Public-meeting benchmark PR/tooling.** Add pinned AMI/ICSI loaders, keep the corpora outside ordinary repository history, freeze source/version/hash, use original manual AMI topic segmentation as primary gold, use QMSum for recurrence tests and AMI-ME as a supplementary 2026 dataset. Embed each transcript once using the packaged E5 encoder.

4. **Algorithm bake-off.** Keep the current pipeline as baseline and compare: current local peaks; length-aware semantic weighting; global CVS-like dynamic-programming segmentation; two-stage local boundary refinement; richer speaker-distribution features; keyword cohesion; current online clustering vs global agglomerative clustering with a low-cohesion split/refinement pass. Nothing becomes production based only on one benchmark.

5. **Derived embedding cache.** Once transcript fingerprinting exists, persist an evictable embedding artifact so threshold/segmentation/clustering experiments don't require another model run. This substantially reduces iteration cost.

6. **Model-independent audio decode spike.** Stream a sealed recording into bounded timestamped decoded audio frames with a fake sink. Test long recordings, pause/resume, cancellation, mic/tab separation and recovery. Do not yet commit to sample rate, VAD, chunk overlap or model-specific preprocessing.

7. **Only then do the ASR bake-off and your in-domain calibration.** Compare candidate recognizers on Russian/Ukrainian/English real extension audio, but judge them on both ASR fidelity and **downstream topic stability**. Once your own hand-labeled conversations exist, use them as the final holdout before freezing the semantic values.

That is the point at which I would decide whether `.93/.95`, four-turn windows, 3-second pauses, current importance weights, etc. become actual product contracts.

