# 25. What I would deliberately *not* change yet

I would leave the current `.93/.95` assignment/merge thresholds as candidates. I would not retune them from English AMI and claim they are valid for Russian/Ukrainian.

I would not change the five importance weights from intuition.

I would not add an LLM.

I would not introduce a generic GPU-resource scheduler until a second heavy model actually exists.

I would not hard-code ASR-specific 16 kHz/VAD/chunk-overlap policies into the generic audio layer.

I would not replace multilingual-E5 based on MTEB alone.

I would not replace the production segmentation/clustering implementation with an academic algorithm until the same corpus runner demonstrates a consistent advantage and the browser cost is measured.

And I would not create a web of `SegmentationStrategy`, `ClusterStrategy`, `KeywordStrategy`, etc. interfaces in production preemptively. Keep algorithm challengers under the calibration/research boundary until one actually wins. That avoids speculative architecture.

